     2	
     3	This vertical completes the direct-TLS/trusted-proxy and bounded-request portions of WN5, WN7,
     4	WN8, and WN9. It wraps the existing command, session-lifecycle, and SSE authority; it does not
     5	introduce another fleet state machine and has no homelab integration.
     6	
     7	## EP1 — canonical client address has one trust boundary
     8	
     9	Direct requests use the socket peer address. Forwarded address headers are ignored unless the
    10	immediate peer exactly matches an explicitly configured trusted-proxy allowlist. Trusted requests
    11	accept one bounded, strictly parsed forwarding chain and select the configured hop; malformed,
    12	overlong, ambiguous, or mixed forwarding headers fail typed before authentication/provider/body
    13	work. Audit records retain only a presence/classification and a keyed address digest, never the raw
    14	address. Empty proxy trust means direct mode.
    15	
    16	## EP2 — deterministic bounded quota authority
    17	
    18	A dependency-free quota authority enforces fixed-window limits with an injected clock, bounded key
    19	cardinality, deterministic expiry, and no randomness. Separate policies cover unauthenticated login
    20	attempts per canonical address, all HTTP requests per address, authenticated commands per
    21	credential, weighted command cost, stream-ticket issuance, and concurrent connections. Limit
    22	configuration rejects zero, negative, non-integer, unbounded, or internally inconsistent values.
    23	
    24	## EP3 — refusal precedes expensive or privileged work
    25	
    26	The address quota runs before body parsing, identity-provider execution, session mutation, or
    27	coordinator dispatch. Login throttling therefore bounds provider calls. Principal/cost quota runs
    28	after authentication but before durable command admission or dispatch. Refusal returns bounded
    29	`429 rate_limited` plus `Retry-After`, is audited fail closed, and mutates no session, command,
    30	worker, or stream state. Client-supplied IDs cannot choose a quota bucket.
    31	
    32	## EP4 — trusted-proxy and TLS modes are explicit
    33	
    34	Direct production mode requires TLS on the accepted socket. Proxy mode may accept a cleartext
    35	backend socket only when the immediate peer is trusted and an exact configured forwarding signal
    36	proves the original request was HTTPS. Untrusted `Forwarded`/`X-Forwarded-*` headers never upgrade
    37	transport, alter address quotas, or enter audit identity. The server refuses proxy mode without a
    38	nonempty peer allowlist and refuses direct mode without TLS key/certificate material.
    39	
    40	## EP5 — health and readiness reveal no fleet state
    41	
    42	`GET /healthz` reports only process liveness. `GET /readyz` reports a single ready/not-ready bit and
    43	fails when operational log/coordination authority, session ledger/liveness verification, command
    44	idempotency storage, or admission state is unavailable. Neither endpoint returns worker, task,
    45	repository, credential, provider, path, error, or dependency detail. Readiness probes are
    46	independently quota-bounded.
    47	
    48	## EP6 — graceful shutdown changes admission, not worker truth
    49	
    50	Shutdown atomically stops new login, refresh, command, ticket, and stream admission; readiness
    51	turns false; accepted HTTP responses receive a bounded drain interval; open streams receive a
